<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18439" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flŭĭdus</span></b>  (access. form, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flŭvĭdus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2,
		452</span></i>; <i><span class="en">464</span></i> sq.;
				<i><span class="en">Sedul. Carm. 4, 186</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 58,
			24</span></i>), a, um, adj.
		fluo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>flowing</i>, <i>fluid</i>, <i>moist</i> (mostly <b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug.
			prose; not in Cic. or Caes.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 452</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid tam contrarium est quam terrenum fluido?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 16, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 484</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cruor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					3, 663</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4, 482</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aspiciam fluidos humano sanguine rictus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 168</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alvus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 29 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In opposition to solid or
			firm, <i>soft</i>, <i>slack</i>, <i>lax</i>, <i>languid</i> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluxus, languidus): lacerti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 231</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labor et aestus mollia et fluida Gallorum
					corpora decedere pugna coëgit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 47, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 30, 50, § 95</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestis,</span>”
				<i>flowing</i>, <i>loose</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					41, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Oed. 422</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>dissolving</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 362</span></i>
			.</div>
